The witness check of a subset type or newtype whose constraint does not mention its bound variable (such as `v: int | true`) no longer changes the source location of the declaration's own constraint. Under `--translation-workers`, the Boogie tokens of the modules that import such a type, from which error locations are drawn, no longer depend on whether the declaring module's translation ran first. The same holds for the termination check of a `decreases` clause over an `iset`, which used to set the source location of the shared Boogie literal `false`. See https://github.com/erniecohen/dafny/issues/569.
